publica functio f() -> u8 poscit Hospes {
    redde 0;
}
```

This Exsecutor does not compile. What is wrong and how do I fix it?

```exsecutor
publica functio f(v: acies<u64, 8>) -> u64 {
    quisque i in 0..8
        contrahe s: +
        forma ordinata
    {
        s = v[i];
        rumpe;
    }
    redde s;
}
```

`exsc` rejects this with `EXS-E0342` (`rumpe` inside an iteration carrying a `contrahe`).

It is reported at line 7, column 9, on `rumpe;`.

An early exit makes the result depend on which iterations ran, and under `quisque` that is not even well defined, so `rumpe` inside an iteration that carries a `contrahe` is `EXS-E0342`. If an early-exit fold is wanted, write a `per` loop with an explicit accumulator: it is ordinary sequential code and claims nothing about shape.

Corrected, and accepted by `exsc`:

```exsecutor
publica functio f(v: acies<u64, 8>) -> u64 {
    mutabilis s: u64 = 0;
    per i in 0..8 {
        s = s + v[i];
        si s gt 100 { rumpe; }
    }
    redde s;
}
```

